{
  "recipe_name" : "Cuban Sandwich",
  "instructions":[
    {
        "text": "Start by getting everything ready, and set it out on the counter for at least 30 minutes."
    },
    {
        "text": "Everything should be room temperature, and I mean everything."
    },
    {
        "text": "This allows everything to cook together nicely and get evenly cooked."
    },
    {
        "text": "When you are ready, I recommend getting 2 heavy cast iron skillets out if you have them."
    },
    {
        "text": "The goal is to create a heavy press, and cast iron not only heats really well, but it has the weight you are looking for to press the sandwich."
    },
    {
        "text": "Build your sandwich by adding the pickles to the bottom layer of bread, or if you want to use mustard, spread a light coating of mustard on before adding the pickles."
    },
    {
        "text": "Then add the roasted pork, ham, and top with cheese."
    },
    {
        "text": "Add the top piece of bread and you are ready to cook."
    },
    {
        "text": "Add about one tablespoon of butter to the skillet that is on medium-low heat."
    },
    {
        "text": "Take the sandwich and massage it into the butter."
    },
    {
        "text": "Take another tablespoon of butter and spread it on the top part of the bread."
    },
    {
        "text": "Lay another cast iron skillet on top of the sandwich, and carefully press down."
    },
    {
        "text": "If you do not have the second skillet, you could wrap aluminum foil around a brick, and use that as your press."
    },
    {
        "text": "Be creative, but find a clean, heavy pot or pan to lay on top of the sandwich."
    },
    {
        "text": "Leave the sandwich alone for a few minutes, however monitor the heat."
    },
    {
        "text": "You definitely do not want to burn the bread, so lower the heat a bit if you are concerned."
    },
    {
        "text": "The goal of the sandwich is to build an amazing crust and have the cheese melt."
    },
    {
        "text": "After a few minutes, flip the sandwich over, add the skillet back to the top of the sandwich, give a little press, and cook another few minutes."
    },
    {
        "text": "Remove it from the pan when done."
    },
    {
        "text": "The sandwich is done when the cheese is melted, and your crust is complete."
    },
    {
        "text": "You know the crust is complete when you tap on the sandwich and you get that sound."
    },
    {
        "text": "Youll know the sound, and it is a beautiful one at that."
    },
    {
        "text": "Take the sandwich and let it rest for a few minutes."
    },
    {
        "text": "Then slice it on a diagonal."
    },
    {
        "text": "The result is everything, and a bit more."
    },
    {
        "text": "The exterior is so wonderful, and biting into it you will know first hand why this sandwich is really great."
    },
    {
        "text": "It could be the combination of flavors, or it could be the balanced textures."
    },
    {
        "text": "Whatever it is, the Cuban sandwich is a must make, and what better time to make one than today or tomorrow!"
    },
    {
        "text": "Enjoy."
    }
  ],
