  "instructions":[
    {
      "text": "Trim the visible fat and silver-skin from the flesh side of the duck. If the tenderloins are still on the breasts, leave them on. Don't trim the skin side; simply score the duck skin in a crosshatch pattern to allow the fat to cook out."
